From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:47:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: add a Matrix protocol (prpl-matrix) to the plugin

Register a third prpl, prpl-matrix ("Matrix"), from the same shared
object, on mautrix-go (already in go.mod for mautrix-meta). It lives
here for the same reason as prpl-gometa: two Go c-archives cannot
share one process. All of its identifiers are prefixed matrix/mx.

- login: the username is the Matrix ID. The account's validator app
  (com.palm.app.matrix) normally signs in itself, in the Accounts app,
  and stores the session as the password: "mxoauth:" + base64url(JSON)
  with homeserver, device, tokens and OAuth client, and optionally the
  recovery key (matrix_seed.go). A session the plugin has not taken yet
  replaces its own; once that ends, the login fails with an
  authentication error so Accounts asks to sign in again. Accounts
  that store a plain password log in with it on servers that offer
  m.login.password; the "browser-sign-in" marker uses the device
  authorization grant on OAuth 2.0 servers (MAS, as on matrix.org):
  the "Matrix" auth conversation shows a link and a code to approve
  in any browser. Tokens, refresh token and device ID are kept in the
  account, so a restart neither asks again nor makes a new device.
- encryption: goolm (pure Go, build tag goolm) on a per-account
  modernc SQLite store, matrix-<user id>.db, wired up without
  mautrix's cryptohelper, which under cgo pulls in mattn/go-sqlite3
  and a second, C, copy of SQLite.
- verification: after the first sync the device's trust is checked.
  An unverified device uses the recovery key from the sign-in once, if
  one came with it, or else asks for the recovery key or passphrase (signs
  the device from secret storage and restores the key backup), or
  VERIFY for emoji verification with another of the user's own
  sessions, after which the backup key is requested over secret
  sharing. Keys received later are backed up every two minutes. A
  message whose key never arrives is fetched from the backup, or
  shown as undecryptable instead of being dropped.
- messages: direct chats (m.direct) as 1:1 conversations, other rooms
  as chats; text, emotes, replies with quotes, edits, deletions,
  reactions both ways, typing, read receipts both ways, invitations to
  direct chats accepted; pictures, video, voice notes and files both
  ways, encrypted in encrypted rooms. Only messages newer than the
  account's first login are shown, so history is not replayed.
- the auth conversation is matched without regard to case: the
  transport stores its address as "matrix".
- glue/init.c and glue/login.c route account removal and webOS
  reactions to it. Removing an account ends its session on the server
  (revoked at the authorization server for an OAuth sign-in, logged out
  otherwise), from the session saved in the account, as libpurple has
  closed the connection by then, and deletes its store. A session
  replaced by a new sign-in in Accounts is ended the same way.

prpl-matrix is also the id of matrix-org's purple-matrix, which this
replaces; only one of the two can register.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS addition, not part of purple-gowhatsapp]
